          "kicker": "Coaching appointment",
          "heading": "Jake White named Fiji head coach, replacing interim Senirusi Seruvakula",
          "body": "Jake White has been named Fiji head coach, succeeding interim coach Senirusi Seruvakula, after being chosen from 31 applicants last week. The 62-year-old was the Bulls' director of rugby from 2020 to 2025, and former Bulls colleagues believe Fiji have found the right man. White inherits a team ranked 10th in the world that has lost four of five Tests this year, and his first match in charge is against Japan. Fiji sit in Pool C at the 2027 World Cup."
